    "final_message": "I built the Everbloom app with Whisker 0.16 in the project root, and it passes every item on the Done checklist I could check here. The one thing I couldn't test is device code signing, because there's no Apple team on this machine. The device build compiles with signing disabled, and the signed command is in `BUILD.md`.\n\n**What I checked**\n- **iOS Simulator (Release build):** I drove the installed app with an XCUITest harness I built in the scratchpad.\n  - Home loads.\n  - A collection opens and scrolls to the end (84 products, loaded 24 at a time), and all four sorts reorder it.\n  - Search returns \"67 results\" and scrolls to the last one.\n  - A product opens, its option pills switch the variant, and a recommendation opens another product with the back button returning to the first.\n  - Add to cart switches to the Cart tab and shows the badge. The stepper moves the badge 1\u21922\u21921 and the subtotal $75\u2192$150\u2192$75. Going to 0 removes the line and shows the empty-cart state.\n  - Check out opens the checkout URL in the in-app Safari view.\n- **Accessibility identifiers:** they show up in the XCUITest tree, and the ones the flow uses resolve to a single element. `search-input` is on the native text field itself.\n- **Log marker:** `SHOPBENCH home_ready` appears exactly once per launch in the simulator log stream.\n- **Error state:** pointed at an unreachable plain-HTTP endpoint through `SHOP_API_URL`, Home shows \"Couldn't load products\". After I started a local proxy, Retry loaded Home. This also confirms the endpoint override and plain HTTP work.\n- **iOS device:** the Release arm64 build succeeds with signing disabled (5.3 MB `.app`). The Info.plist has the 120 Hz key and the plain-HTTP permission.\n- **Android:** a signed release APK installs and runs on the emulator, and Home loads.\n\n**Decisions worth knowing**\n- **Small native module (`shop-native/`):** Whisker has no HTTP client, timer, alert or system log, so I wrote one in Swift and Kotlin using the platforms' own HTTP. It also adds the Info.plist keys at generation time. Apart from Whisker's own crates, the only added dependencies are `serde`/`serde_json`, which Whisker already pulls in.\n- **Covered screens hidden from accessibility:** Whisker's router keeps the screens underneath mounted. Without a fix, `back` and `add-to-cart` matched twice after opening a product from a recommendation. A wrapper now hides covered screens, so each identifier matches one element.\n- **Search screen:** the results shrink above the keyboard, and dragging them dismisses it. Without this, swipes on `search-results` while the keyboard was up started under the keyboard and didn't scroll.\n- **Left out or not met:** I didn't implement the design's \"See all\" link, because the spec gives it no destination. Android isn't locked to portrait, because Whisker's configuration has no setting for it.\n\nAll the spec-silent choices and every dependency are listed in `NOTES.md`. `BUILD.md` has the clean-checkout commands, output paths, build modes and toolchain versions."
